<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.378 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.378 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.5 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due October 23 was 3.378 percent, up from 3.206 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 175-day T-bills due January 15, 1998, was 3.769 percent, up from 3.55 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due July 23, 1998 was 4.264 percent, up from 4.162 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$775 million of C$4.9 billion bills due July 31. (Details follow)  </p>
